    "bio": "A Representative from Minnesota; born in Fargo, Cass County, N.D., June 29, 1944; B.A., Moorhead State University, Moorhead, Minn., 1966; United States Army National Guard, 1963-1969; certified public accountant; member of the Minnesota state senate, 1977-1986; unsuccessful candidate for election to the Ninety-ninth Congress in 1984 and to the One Hundredth Congress in 1986; unsuccessful candidate for nomination to the One Hundred First Congress in 1988; elected as a Democrat to the One Hundred Second and to the fourteen succeeding Congresses (January 3, 1991-January 3, 2021); unsuccessful candidate for reelection to the One Hundred Seventeenth Congress in 2020; chair, Committee on Agriculture (One Hundred Tenth, One Hundred Eleventh, and One Hundred Sixteenth Congresses).",
